**Part 1: macOS TIFF-only pasteboard reports no image.**
`_readMacos` only tries `«class PNGf»` and `«class JPEG»`. Fix: add a fallback `«class TIFF»` read, then convert TIFF to PNG via `sips -s format png <in> --out <out>`, and return as `PasteboardImage`. If the conversion fails, fall through to `PasteboardUnavailable`.

**Part 2: UX gap — Ctrl+V with a TEXT clipboard does nothing useful.**
`_handlePasteImageKey` fires the image probe and, on failure, prints the reason. The ticket says: "On probe failure with a text clipboard, Ctrl+V should insert the clipboard text (via `pbpaste` / the platform reader) into the composer."

So we need:
1. A "read clipboard text" function in `clipboard_reader.dart` — e.g. `readPasteboardText()` — using `pbpaste` on macOS, `xclip -selection clipboard -o` / `wl-paste` on Linux, `powershell Get-Clipboard` on Windows. With the injectable `ProcessRunner` seam.
2. Wire a `readClipboardText` callback in `FaTuiCallbacks` and `agent_cli_repl_boot.dart`.
3. In `_handlePasteboardResult` (or `_handlePasteImageKey`), when the probe fails AND there's text available, insert the text into the composer.

