## RCA

**Bug**: macOS clipboard image reads fail when the pasteboard holds only TIFF; Ctrl+V with a text clipboard does nothing useful.

**Root cause**:
1. `lib/src/cli/clipboard_reader.dart` `_readMacos` tries only `«class PNGf»` and `«class JPEG»`. Apps like Preview/browsers put TIFF (`«class TIFF»`) on the pasteboard, so both probes fail → `PasteboardUnavailable('clipboard holds no image')`.
2. `fa_tui_paste.dart` `_handlePasteImageKey` fires only the image probe; on failure it prints the reason. Nothing reads clipboard TEXT on Ctrl+V, so a text clipboard pastes nothing.

**Fix approach**:
1. `_readMacos`: after PNGf and JPEG fail, try `«class TIFF»` → write to a `.tiff` scratch file → convert to PNG with `sips -s format png <in> --out <out>` → read the PNG bytes → return `PasteboardImage(pngBytes)`. Conversion failure → fall through to `PasteboardUnavailable`. Clean up scratch files.
2. Add `readPasteboardText` platform glue (pbpaste / xclip / wl-paste / PowerShell Get-Clipboard) behind the same injectable `ProcessRunner` seam.
3. Add `readClipboardText` to `FaTuiCallbacks` (real + stub + web stub), wire in `agent_cli_repl_boot.dart`.
4. In the Ctrl+V flow: when the image probe returns non-image and a text reader is wired, fire a text read; if text arrives, deliver it as a `PasteMsg` (reuses existing insertion, mojibake fixing, prompt routing); else print the original named reason.

