Also the ticket says the UX fix: "On probe failure with a text clipboard, Ctrl+V should insert the clipboard text (via `pbpaste` / the platform reader) into the composer." — composer, i.e., normal mode. Prompt mode: not required (minimal fix). But hmm — if the PasteMsg fallback lands while a prompt opened in between... `_handlePaste` handles `prompt != null` by routing to the prompt buffer — that's existing behavior, fine.

