```

The type of `_firePasteboardProbe`'s reader is `Future<PasteboardRead> Function()`. Returning `PasteMsg` from it doesn't type-check. Hmm.

So the Cmd must be allowed to return a different Msg. Let me look at `_pasteboardProbe`:

```dart
Cmd _pasteboardProbe(Future<PasteboardRead> Function() reader, {required bool silentFailure}) =>
    () async => PasteboardResultMsg(await reader(), silentFailure: silentFailure);
```

Options:
- Add a `PasteboardText` variant into `PasteboardRead` (sealed) and have `_handlePasteboardResult` handle a `PasteboardText` result by inserting text into the editor. That keeps ONE message type and the sealed-family pattern. 

That's clean! Add to `paste_image.dart`:

```dart
/// Text clipboard content (gh-1575): the Ctrl+V image probe falls back to
/// the platform text reader when the pasteboard holds no image. The TUI
/// inserts [text] into the composer.
final class PasteboardText extends PasteboardRead {
  const PasteboardText(this.text);
  final String text;
}
```

Then the Ctrl+V wrapped reader returns `PasteboardText(text)` on image-miss + text-hit, and `_handlePasteboardResult` handles `read is PasteboardText` by inserting text (with `_fixPasteMojibake`? No — pbpaste output is proper UTF-8 from our byte decode; no mojibake. Just insert).

In `_handlePasteboardResult`:

```dart
